  "argv": [
    "claude",
    "-p",
    "Bug report for this repository (rich):\n\n`Table(highlight=True)` highlights the cells of columns declared with `add_column`, but when a\nrow passed to `add_row` has more cells than there are columns, the columns created on the fly\nfor the extra cells do not inherit the table's `highlight` setting \u2014 `table.columns[i].highlight`\nis `False` for them, and their cells render unhighlighted (a `repr` string such as `'FOO'` is\nnot coloured, while the same cell in a declared column is).\n\nFix it so that columns created by `add_row` take the table's `highlight` value.\n\nChange as little as possible and do not edit the tests. The test command is\n`python -m pytest -q tests/test_table.py`; run it once at the end.",
